#: ../pwntools/docs/source/about.rst:2
msgid "About pwntools"
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/source/about.rst:4
msgid ""
"Whether you're using it to write exploits, or as part of another software"
" project will dictate how you use it."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/source/about.rst:7
msgid ""
"Historically pwntools was used as a sort of exploit-writing DSL. Simply "
"doing ``from pwn import *`` in a previous version of pwntools would bring"
" all sorts of nice side-effects."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/source/about.rst:11
msgid "When redesigning pwntools for 2.0, we noticed two contrary goals:"
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/source/about.rst:13
msgid ""
"We would like to have a \"normal\" python module structure, to allow "
"other people to familiarize themselves with pwntools quickly."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/source/about.rst:15
msgid ""
"We would like to have even more side-effects, especially by putting the "
"terminal in raw-mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/source/about.rst:18
msgid ""
"To make this possible, we decided to have two different modules. "
":mod:`pwnlib` would be our nice, clean Python module, while :mod:`pwn` "
"would be used during CTFs."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/source/about.rst:23
msgid ":mod:`pwn` --- Toolbox optimized for CTFs"
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/source/about.rst:27
msgid ""
"As stated, we would also like to have the ability to get a lot of these "
"side-effects by default. That is the purpose of this module. It does the "
"following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/source/about.rst:31
msgid ""
"Imports everything from the toplevel :mod:`pwnlib` along with functions "
"from a lot of submodules. This means that if you do ``import pwn`` or "
"``from pwn import *``, you will have access to everything you need to "
"write an exploit."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/source/about.rst:35
msgid ""
"Calls :func:`pwnlib.term.init` to put your terminal in raw mode and "
"implements functionality to make it appear like it isn't."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/source/about.rst:37
msgid "Setting the :data:`pwnlib.context.log_level` to `\"info\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/source/about.rst:38
msgid ""
"Tries to parse some of the values in :data:`sys.argv` and every value it "
"succeeds in parsing it removes."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/source/about.rst:42
msgid ":mod:`pwnlib` --- Normal python library"
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/source/about.rst:46
msgid ""
"This module is our \"clean\" python-code. As a rule, we do not think that"
" importing :mod:`pwnlib` or any of the submodules should have any "
"significant side-effects (besides e.g. caching)."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/source/about.rst:50
msgid ""
"For the most part, you will also only get the bits you import. You for "
"instance would not get access to :mod:`pwnlib.util.packing` simply by "
"doing ``import pwnlib.util``."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/source/about.rst:54
msgid ""
"Though there are a few exceptions (such as :mod:`pwnlib.shellcraft`), "
"that does not quite fit the goals of being simple and clean, but they can"
" still be imported without implicit side-effects."
msgstr ""

